  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8FC4A7">Example <span data-tag="8FC4A7">5.2.7.10</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category which has a final object, and let $\calC ^{0}$ be the full subcategory of $\calC $ spanned by the final objects. Then the inclusion $\calC ^{0} \subseteq \calC $ admits a left adjoint. </p>
